  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (0.485–0.650) over image-only (0.208). Within RNA, multiprofile+avgpool consistently outperforms singleprofile or transformer aggregation (config_002: 0.591 > config_001: 0.485; config_002: 0.591 > config_003: 0.519). The encoder swap from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (config_005 vs config_002) yielded the largest single gain (+5.9 pp to 0.650), making encoder choice the most impactful design axis. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested scgpt, the third available RNA encoder. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 under the same multiprofile+avgpool setting? config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), isolating the encoder effect. Why best next: The encoder is the highest-leverage choice identified so far, and resolving whether scgpt beats scvi_n200 will (a) establish the best RNA backbone, (b) inform which encoder to pair with image in any future multimodal experiments, and (c) avoid committing multiple future experiments to a suboptimal encoder. Testing transformer aggregation with scvi_n200 (config_006) is lower priority since avgpool already showed a consistent advantage over transformer with pca_n2000."
}

